    <description>The Apollo 17 Lunar Seismic Profiling Experiment (LSPE) measured the seismic signals produced by the detonation of eight explosive charges on the surface by using a network of four geophones. 
            Following this active experiment, the experiment became a passive seismometer, measuring the natural seismic activity resulting from moonquakes or meteorite impacts.</description>
